WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.174
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.474 --> 00:00:09.907
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:16.331
Unit twelve: Relative Clauses. Today you will add information using who, which, that and whose.

4
00:00:16.631 --> 00:00:19.190
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.494
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.653
Relative pronoun.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.660
Relative pronoun means a word like who or which.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.936
Who is a relative pronoun.

9
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.620
Your turn. Say: Relative pronoun.

10
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.025
Relative pronoun.

11
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:41.355
Who.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.850
Who means used for people.

13
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.624
The girl who sings is my sister.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.486
Your turn. Say: Who.

15
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.009
Who.

16
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.589
Which.

17
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.200
Which means used for things.

18
00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:59.458
The book which I bought is new.

19
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.342
Your turn. Say: Which.

20
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.004
Which.

21
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.542
That.

22
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.851
That means used for people or things.

23
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.055
The car that I like is red.

24
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.954
Your turn. Say: That.

25
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.464
That.

26
00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:20.997
Whose.

27
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.936
Whose means used to show belonging.

28
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.863
The boy whose bag is lost is crying.

29
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.975
Your turn. Say: Whose.

30
00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:33.649
Whose.

31
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:35.257
Where.

32
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.168
Where means used for places.

33
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:40.388
The town where I live is small.

34
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:43.682
Your turn. Say: Where.

35
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:48.196
Where.

36
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.009
Defining.

37
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.643
Defining means giving necessary information.

38
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.563
A defining clause has no commas.

39
00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.535
Your turn. Say: Defining.

40
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.401
Defining.

41
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.302
Non-defining.

42
00:02:06.317 --> 00:02:09.106
Non-defining means giving extra information.

43
00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:11.960
A non-defining clause uses commas.

44
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.481
Your turn. Say: Non-defining.

45
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:19.520
Non-defining.

46
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:23.973
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.817 --> 00:02:26.839
Visal, what are relative clauses?

48
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:38.021
They give more information about a noun. We use who for people, which for things, that for both, whose for belonging and where for places.

49
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.884
What is a defining clause?

50
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:51.172
It gives necessary information and has no commas: The student who sits next to me is Dara. Without it, we do not know which student.

51
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:54.167
And a non-defining clause?

52
00:02:55.283 --> 00:03:04.310
It gives extra information with commas: Angkor Wat, which is in Siem Reap, is famous. We cannot use that in a non-defining clause.

53
00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:06.874
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.717 --> 00:03:12.468
Grammar focus: Relative clause: noun plus who and which and that plus verb.

55
00:03:12.768 --> 00:03:13.920
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:16.547
The girl who sings is my sister.

57
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.518
Angkor Wat, which is in Siem Reap, is famous.

58
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:28.322
Use who for people, which for things, whose for belonging and where for places. Use commas for extra information.

59
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.606
Be careful! Don't say: The girl which sings is my sister.

60
00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.961
Say: The girl who sings is my sister.

61
00:03:37.261 --> 00:03:38.750
Use who for people.

62
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:42.476
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.243
Describing People and Places.

64
00:03:45.543 --> 00:03:48.332
The teacher who teaches us English is very kind.

65
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:51.263
The book that she lent me is interesting.

66
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.684
The village where I was born is near a river.

67
00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.535
My neighbour, whose house is next to ours, is a farmer.

68
00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:02.624
Angkor Wat, which is in Siem Reap, is a famous temple.

69
00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:08.107
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.159
The girl blank sings is my sister.

71
00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:14.648
A, who. B, which. C, where.

72
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.060
The answer is A: who.

73
00:04:21.217 --> 00:04:22.856
The book blank I bought is new.

74
00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:26.299
A, whose. B, which. C, who.

75
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:31.937
The answer is B: which.

76
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:34.944
The town blank I live is small.

77
00:04:35.244 --> 00:04:38.746
A, who. B, which. C, where.

78
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.125
The answer is C: where.

79
00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:47.863
Extra information is put between blank.

80
00:04:48.163 --> 00:04:52.003
A, commas. B, brackets only. C, nothing.

81
00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.450
The answer is A: commas.

82
00:04:58.617 --> 00:04:59.966
Whose shows blank.

83
00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:03.989
A, time. B, belonging. C, place.

84
00:05:07.533 --> 00:05:09.614
The answer is B: belonging.

85
00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.975
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.817 --> 00:05:18.128
Describe a person you admire using a relative clause.

87
00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:28.336
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.636 --> 00:05:37.560
I admire my teacher who helps students after class. She is a person who never gives up. The school where she works is lucky to have her.

89
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.604
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.517 --> 00:05:47.337
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clause: noun plus who and which and that plus verb.

91
00:05:47.637 --> 00:05:52.878
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

92
00:05:53.178 --> 00:05:56.191
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:56.491 --> 00:05:59.224
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

